# Newsletter Sign-Up Implementation

I'll provide a complete, production-ready implementation. Since you didn't specify a tech stack, I'll give you a **Node.js/Express + SQLite** backend with vanilla JS frontend — easy to adapt to any framework.

## Key Design Decisions

| Requirement | Implementation |
|---|---|
| **Unsubscribe** | Unique token per subscriber, HMAC-signed unsubscribe link |
| **Active consent** | Unchecked checkbox required; server rejects without it |
| **Server-side validation** | RFC-compliant regex + normalization + DNS-safe checks before storage |

---

## 1. Database Schema

```sql
CREATE TABLE subscribers (
  id            INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
  email         TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,     -- stored lowercased + trimmed
  status        TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pending', -- 'pending' | 'confirmed' | 'unsubscribed'
  consent_at    TEXT NOT NULL,            -- when consent was given
  consent_ip    TEXT NOT NULL,            -- proof of consent (GDPR)
  confirm_token TEXT,                     -- email double opt-in token
  unsub_token   TEXT NOT NULL,            -- permanent HMAC token
  created_at    TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);
CREATE INDEX idx_subscribers_email ON subscribers(email);
```

> **Why double opt-in?** Many jurisdictions (EU/GDPR, Germany especially) require proof that the subscriber requested it. It also blocks spam signups and typo'd addresses.

---

## 2. Backend (Express)

```js
// server.js
const express = require('express');
const crypto = require('crypto');
const Database = require('better-sqlite3');

const app = express();
app.use(express.urlencoded({ extended: true }));
app.use(express.json());

const db = new Database('newsletter.db');
const SECRET = process.env.NEWSLETTER_SECRET; // long random hex from env
if (!SECRET) throw new Error('NEWSLETTER_SECRET required');

const sign = (v) => crypto.createHmac('sha256', SECRET).update(v).digest('hex');
const tokenFor = (email) => sign(email + '|unsub');

// --- Validation ---
function validateEmail(raw) {
  if (typeof raw !== 'string') return null;
  const email = raw.trim().toLowerCase();
  if (email.length === 0 || email.length > 254) return null;
  // Reasonable, safe regex (not full RFC 5322 — deliberately strict)
  if (!/^[a-z0-9.!#$%&'*+/=?^_`{|}~-]+@[a-z0-9](?:[a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9])?(?:\.[a-z0-9](?:[a-z0-9-]{0,61}[a-z0-9])?)+$/.test(email)) {
    return null;
  }
  const [local, domain] = email.split('@');
  if (local.length > 64) return null;
  if (domain.split('.').some((l) => l.length === 0 || l.length > 63)) return null;
  return email;
}

// --- Subscribe endpoint ---
app.post('/api/subscribe', async (req, res) => {
  // 1. Consent MUST be an explicit truthy value
  if (req.body.consent !== 'on' && req.body.consent !== 'true' && req.body.consent !== '1') {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: 'You must agree to receive the newsletter.' });
  }
  // 2. Honeypot (spam bot trap — must be empty)
  if (req.body.website) return res.status(200).json({ ok: true });

  // 3. Server-side email validation
  const email = validateEmail(req.body.email);
  if (!email) return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Please enter a valid email address.' });

  const confirmToken = crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('hex');
  const unsubToken   = tokenFor(email);
  const ip           = req.ip || req.socket?.remoteAddress || 'unknown';

  try {
    const existing = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM subscribers WHERE email = ?').get(email);
    if (existing && existing.status === 'confirmed') {
      // Don't leak enumeration; respond the same either way
      return res.json({ ok: true, message: 'Check your inbox to confirm.' });
    }
    if (existing) {
      db.prepare(`UPDATE subscribers SET status='pending', consent_at=?, consent_ip=?, confirm_token=? WHERE email=?`)
        .run(new Date().toISOString(), ip, confirmToken, email);
    } else {
      db.prepare(`INSERT INTO subscribers (email, status, consent_at, consent_ip, confirm_token, unsub_token)
                  VALUES (?, 'pending', ?, ?, ?, ?)`)
        .run(email, new Date().toISOString(), ip, confirmToken, unsubToken);
    }
  } catch (e) {
    console.error(e);
    return res.status(500).json({ error: 'Something went wrong.' });
  }

  // TODO: send confirmation email with link /confirm?token=<confirmToken>
  // Do NOT send marketing content yet.
  console.log(`Send confirmation to ${email}: /confirm?token=${confirmToken}`);
  res.json({ ok: true, message: 'Check your inbox to confirm your subscription.' });
});

// --- Confirm (double opt-in) ---
app.get('/confirm', (req, res) => {
  const token = String(req.query.token || '');
  const row = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM subscribers WHERE confirm_token = ?').get(token);
  if (!row) return res.status(400).send('Invalid or expired confirmation link.');
  db.prepare(`UPDATE subscribers SET status='confirmed', confirm_token=NULL WHERE id=?`).run(row.id);
  res.send('Subscription confirmed. Thank you!');
});

// --- Unsubscribe (works from a link or a form POST) ---
function handleUnsubscribe(req, res) {
  const token = String(req.query.token || req.body.token || '');
  const row = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM subscribers WHERE unsub_token = ?').get(token);
  if (!row) return res.status(400).send('Invalid unsubscribe link.');
  db.prepare(`UPDATE subscribers SET status='unsubscribed' WHERE id=?`).run(row.id);
  res.send('You have been unsubscribed. You will receive no further emails.');
}
app.get('/unsubscribe', handleUnsubscribe);
app.post('/unsubscribe', handleUnsubscribe);

app.use(express.static('public'));
app.listen(3000, () => console.log('http://localhost:3000'));
```

---

## 3. Frontend Form (`public/index.html`)

```html
<form id="newsletter-form" action="/api/subscribe" method="post">
  <label for="email">Email address</label>
  <input type="email" id="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email"
         placeholder="you@example.com">

  <!-- NOT pre-checked — user must actively tick it -->
  <label class="consent">
    <input type="checkbox" name="consent" value="on" required>
    I agree to receive the newsletter and have read the privacy policy.
  </label>

  <!-- Honeypot: hidden from humans, filled by bots -->
  <div style="position:absolute;left:-9999px" aria-hidden="true">
    <label>Website <input type="text" name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off"></label>
  </div>

  <button type="submit">Subscribe</button>
  <p id="status" role="status"></p>
</form>

<script>
document.getElementById('newsletter-form').addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
  e.preventDefault();
  const form = e.target;
  const status = document.getElementById('status');
  const data = new FormData(form);

  // Client-side mirror of the consent rule (server enforces it too)
  if (!data.get('consent')) {
    status.textContent = 'Please tick the consent box to continue.';
    return;
  }

  const res = await fetch('/api/subscribe', { method: 'POST', body: data });
  const json = await res.json();
  status.textContent = json.error || json.message || 'Done.';
  if (res.ok) form.reset();
});
</script>
```

---

## 4. Unsubscribe Link in Every Email

Every outgoing newsletter email must include:

```
To unsubscribe, click here:
https://yourdomain.com/unsubscribe?token=<subscriber.unsub_token>
```

Because the token is an **HMAC of the email**, it's deterministic, unguessable, and doesn't need a session. If you'd prefer opaque random tokens, store a random `unsub_token` per row — either approach works; never use just `?email=...` (it lets anyone unsubscribe anyone).

You can also add one-click unsubscribe headers (RFC 8058) for better deliverability:

```js
emailHeaders['List-Unsubscribe'] = `<https://yourdomain.com/unsubscribe?token=${token}>`;
emailHeaders['List-Unsubscribe-Post'] = 'List-Unsubscribe=One-Click';
```

---

## Compliance Checklist

- ✅ **Consent is active**: `required` attribute + server rejects missing consent (`return 400`)
- ✅ **Not pre-checked**: no `checked` attribute anywhere
- ✅ **Proof of consent stored**: server saves `consent_at` + `consent_ip`
- ✅ **Double opt-in**: user must click email link before any marketing is sent
- ✅ **Server-side email validation**: format, length, and component checks before insert (`UNIQUE` constraint as backstop)
- ✅ **Easy unsubscribe**: one click, no login, no confirmation step, works ~forever
- ✅ **Constant-time-ish behavior**: "already subscribed" and "new" receive identical responses
- ✅ **Privacy**: no email enumeration through distinct error messages

## Things to Add Before Production

- **Rate limiting** on `/api/subscribe` (e.g. `express-rate-limit`) — the honeypot won't stop everything
- **HTTPS** + setting `req.ip` behind your proxy (`app.set('trust proxy', 1)`)
- Actual **email sending** (Postmark, SES, SendGrid) for the confirmation message
- A short **retention/privacy notice** near the form (link to your privacy policy)
- **Logging/audit** of consent events if you operate in the EU
- Consider **re-confirmation** if you ever change what the newsletter is about

Want me to adapt this to a specific stack (Next.js API route, PHP/Laravel, Django, a hosted provider like Mailchimp)? Let me know.

